        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4837_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4837_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4837_Start4" name="JV/consortium bid (large B2G/project); foreign-contractor partnership; capacity gap…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4837_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4837_Task5" name="Evaluate JV/consortium/foreign-partner licensing: where BuildRight lacks the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Evaluate JV/consortium/foreign-partner licensing: where BuildRight lacks the category/capacity (W4819) or specialty scope, partner with a licensed contractor or foreign contractor (links to VS-160 immigration/mobility for seconded experts); assess the partner&#x27;s PCAB license, TPRM (VS-161), and the JV legal structure
Responsible (R): PCAB Compliance Lead / Legal / Strategy / Trade Sales
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance / COO
Duration: Per opportunity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4837_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4837_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4837_Task6" name="Structure the JV/consortium license compliance: which entity is the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Structure the JV/consortium license compliance: which entity is the contractor-of-record, license-applicability of the JV entity (new/special PCAB registration if a JV entity is formed), lead-member vs equal share, scope allocation, and flow-down (W4829); contract via Legal (VS-100.3)
Responsible (R): Legal / PCAB Compliance Lead / Corporate Development
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per opportunity</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4837_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4837_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4837_Task7" name="Govern the JV/consortium during execution: license currency of all members…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govern the JV/consortium during execution: license currency of all members, performance/compliance (W4834), payment security (W4831), and closeout (W4832); manage foreign-contractor PCAB/special-permit and visa (VS-160) compliance; feed JV economics to analytics (W4839)
Responsible (R): PCAB Compliance Lead / Legal / Trade Sales
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4837_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4837_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4837_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4837_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4837_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-727 (ensure controlled execution — Contractor Compliance, Inspection Response &amp; Analytics (PA-165.3).) | - CTL-727: JV/consortium members PCAB-licensed; contractor-of-record defined; foreign-staff compliant (VS-160); flow-down in JV agreement
Owner: VP Legal &amp; Compliance / PCAB Compliance Lead / Strategy (VS-33)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
